      "turn": 1,
      "doctor_question": "Hello, welcome. What brings you in to see me today?",
      "targeted_symptom": "S019",
      "patient_response": "Well, I... I came in because I just can't shake this feeling lately. It's at work—I'm a teacher, secondary school, mostly history and a little geography when they need me to fill in. But anyway, it's the staff emails and the morning announcements. I just know they're actually coded messages about me. My colleagues, they try to be gentle about it, you know, they show me the emails and say, \"Look, this went to the whole staff list,\" but... it doesn't change what I know is there. It's like that time I found a stray cat near the cafeteria, just wandering around by the bins. It had this little bell on its collar that kept ringing, and I spent half my lunch break trying to catch it before the kids got out. The principal was so annoyed, but I couldn't just leave it there. Anyway, the emails... they just feel so pointed, even if everyone else's name is on the \"To\" line.",
