    {
      "turn": 2,
      "doctor_question": "About how long have you been feeling that these emails and announcements are directed at you?",
      "targeted_symptom": "psychotic_symptoms_duration",
      "patient_response": "Well, let me think... it's been about four months now. Right around the time we had the autumn half-term. I remember because the weather turned so quickly this year, didn't it? One week we were all still in our light jackets, and the next, the heating completely broke down in the humanities block. It was absolutely freezing. I had to bring in this little portable space heater from home, the one I usually keep in the conservatory. But the site manager, Dave—he’s a lovely man, but very strict on health and safety—he came right into my classroom and told me I couldn't use it. He actually confiscated it and put it in his office, which was a bit ridiculous because his office is always boiling anyway. \n\nBut, oh, anyway, yes... about four months. That's how long the worries about the coded messages have been going on. And... well, it's been about that long for the voice, too. The one I sometimes answer. It all sort of started right around the time Dave took my heater, actually. I just remember standing there feeling so terribly cold while I was trying to read the morning bulletin...",
