    {
      "turn": 3,
      "doctor_question": "Over these past four months, how has your mood generally been?",
      "targeted_symptom": null,
      "patient_response": "My mood? Well, I haven't really noticed a change in my mood, to be honest. I suppose I've just felt... fine? Normal, really. Just terribly busy. I mean, as normal as you can feel when you're trying to get Year 9s to actually care about the Industrial Revolution. \n\nWe just started the unit on the textile industry last week, and I actually bought some raw cotton off the internet to pass around the class. I thought it would be a nice tactile experience for them, you know? Bring history to life a bit. But half of them just pulled it apart and started throwing it at each other when my back was turned. One boy, Thomas—he's a bright lad but absolutely no impulse control—he managed to flick a clump of it right up onto the projector lens. It started smoking after a few minutes, and the smell was absolutely terrible, like burnt hair. We had to open all the windows, which completely defeated the whole purpose of getting the heating fixed in the first place. The IT technician, poor Gareth, had to come in with a stepladder right in the middle of my lesson to scrape it off. \n\nSo, yes, it's just been the usual sort of chaos, really. I haven't had much time to sit and think about how I'm feeling. What were you asking me again? Something about the term?",
